Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: make the WinRT probe test the header its sources need

The winapi_app branch compiles gstd3d11window_corewindow.cpp and
gstd3d11window_swapchainpanel.cpp, both of which include
<windows.ui.xaml.media.dxinterop.h>. The feature probe that enables that branch
does not, so on a toolchain that ships the WinRT headers but not that one the
probe succeeds and the build then fails:

  gstd3d11window_corewindow.cpp:32:10: fatal error:
      windows.ui.xaml.media.dxinterop.h: No such file or directory

mingw-w64 is exactly that toolchain: it has windows.ui.xaml.h,
windows.ui.xaml.interop.h and the rest, but not the dxinterop one. And
WINAPI_PARTITION_APP is true for desktop targets, so nothing else in the probe
rejects it. MSVC is unaffected, which is why upstream CI does not see this.

Adding the header to the probe makes it fail where the sources would fail,
leaving d3d11 desktop support (screen capture, win32 window) fully enabled and
skipping only the two UWP window backends.
---
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/d3d11/meson.build
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/d3d11/meson.build
@@ -90,6 +90,7 @@
       #include <wrl/wrappers/corewrappers.h>
       #include <d3d11_4.h>
       #include <dxgi1_6.h>
+      #include <windows.ui.xaml.media.dxinterop.h>
       #if !WINAPI_FAMILY_PARTITION(WINAPI_PARTITION_APP)
       #error "not winrt"
       #endif
